= The Market for Proxy Advice

== Concentration

#slide[
  === Two firms advise holders of most of the shares voted at U.S. annual meetings.
  #inv("R1")

  - ISS and Glass Lewis together hold over 90% of the market for proxy advice.

  - Most institutional holders subscribe to at least one of them.
]

#slide[
  === Both advisors sell the research and the machinery that casts the vote.
  #inv("A2")

  - ISS was founded in 1985; Glass Lewis in 2003.

  - Each pairs research reports with a vote-execution platform, so a holder can vote by default.

  - Their benchmark policies are published each November.
]

#slide[
  === A negative ISS recommendation moves support for a say-on-pay proposal by about 25 points.
  #inv("T3")

  - The effect is largest at firms with high institutional ownership.

  - It is smaller where the holder base is retail.
]
